                        class="section_heading">A&nbsp; <em>little about</em> &nbsp;my thought's.</h2>
                    <p id="w-node-_98a14f7d-fdb7-2633-ed68-c96352d5cbba-07f6a17a" class="section_body small about-1"
                        style="transform: translate3d(0px, 0em, 0px) scale3d(1, 1, 1) rotateX(0deg) rotateY(0deg) rotateZ(0deg) skew(0deg, 0deg); transform-style: preserve-3d; opacity: 1;">
                        What I love most about you is this —
                        you are a woman who stands on her own,
                        building something beautiful from nothing,
                        brick by brick, breath by breath.
                        There have been storms, and there have been silences,
                        but you met every one of them with a quiet, unshakeable boldness.
                        You have been wounded — by words, by people, by the noise within —
                        yet here you are, still standing, still healing, still whole.
                        I wish I carried even half your strength.
                        But perhaps that is why you are my anchor —
                        even when the distance stretches between us,
                        even when you may not feel me near,
                        know this with certainty:
                        I am here. I always will be.
